  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Desktop mode, started happening maybe last or recent update and my only clue I've heard it's something to do with EAC or mouse sensitivity. I use 3.2K DPI, but changing the value did not appear to help. The effect is unnoticeable when you begin existing, but it just gets worse. It appears to happen on any world. After a while of existing, the symptoms manifest in full effect.\n\nExample: I join any random world, game operates at 40–60 fps, I shake my mouse really fast side to side and the frames drop completely when the mouse is in motion and the frames are updated only in the far left and right positions of shaking, or the displayed fps goes to 10 or worse. Walking around is entirely smooth but if panning your view with your mouse is introduced to the locomotion, the frame is completely frozen and waits until I stop moving it, and it is updated again, making the effect look like teleporting.\n\nI hope I explained this well. \n\n(attachment size limit) I also recorded and uploaded an unlisted YT video to showcase the effect: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8N7BRIOS5mU\n\nNot recording game or using discord overlay.\n\nI don't think gpu is a problem here, but I did update it not so long ago and maybe the up-to-date one was just caca, so I decided to just try lowering to older gpu driver (from rtx 4060 591.74 game ready driver to 581.57 studio driver.) The issue still manifests the same way within some minutes.\n\nHopefully any of this info is useful and I would provide more if needed.",
